Now I'll create the pre-commit hook that runs mypy on all Python files in `src/`:
======================================================================

======================================================================
                              TOOL CALL                               
======================================================================
Function: execute_command
Arguments: {"command": "cat > .git/hooks/pre-commit << 'EOF'\n#!/bin/sh\n# Run mypy type checking on all Python files in src/\n\n# Get all Python files in src/\nFILES=$(find src/ -name \"*.py\" -type f)\n\n# Exit if no files found\nif [ -z \"$FILES\" ]; then\n    echo \"No Python files found in src/\"\n    exit 0\nfi\n\n# Run mypy with the settings from pyproject.toml\necho \"Running mypy type-checking...\"\nmypy src/\n\n# Check mypy exit code\nif [ $? -ne 0 ]; then\n    echo \"\u274c Type-checking failed. Commit blocked.\"\n    echo \"Please fix the type errors before committing.\"\n    exit 1\nfi\n\n# Run strict mode check as well (redundant but extra safety)\necho \"Running mypy in strict mode for additional checks...\"\nmypy --strict src/\n\nif [ $? -ne 0 ]; then\n    echo \"\u274c Strict type-checking failed. Commit blocked.\"\n    exit 1\nfi\n\necho \"\u2705 Type-checking passed. Proceeding with commit...\"\nexit 0\nEOF"}
